    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="0317" n="1367" xml:id="pg1367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">601.8990D/3–2652: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Merrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d824-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-03-26T15:00:00+04:30">March 26, 1952—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>406. PriMin<anchor n="2" xml:id="d824-f2"/>
                    informed me this morning that an Afghan Amb wld
                    not be sent to Karachi until the Pak Govt had
                    accepted the fourth point of the November 7 proposal.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d824-f3"/> He seemed pleased however that Shah<anchor n="4" xml:id="d824-f4"/> is
                    coming to Kabul as PakAmb and appeared to hope that some good might come of the appt.</p>
                <p>When I told him that while in Wash I had been much disappointed to learn of a
                    recrudescence of Afghan propaganda against Pak
                    he admitted this had occurred but said that “slowly slowly it wld die out”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Merrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d824-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d824-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated for information to London and Karachi.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d824-f2" n="2" xml:id="d824-f2-content">
                <p>Shah Mahmud Ghazi.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d824-f3" n="3" xml:id="d824-f3-content">
                <p>Reference is to the U.S. initiative of Nov. 6, 1950. See <ref target="#d823-f3"
                        >footnote 4, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d824-f4" n="4" xml:id="d824-f4-content">
                <p>Col. A. S. B. Shah.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
